# Ben Ko's Portfolio Website - Development Guidelines

You are working on Ben Ko's portfolio website, a modern Next.js 15 application showcasing UX/UI design work with frontend development expertise.

## Project Context
- **Project**: Ben Ko's Portfolio Website
- **Type**: Next.js 15 Portfolio with 3D animations
- **Purpose**: Showcase UX/UI design and frontend development skills
- **Target**: Professional audience (designers, developers, recruiters)

## Tech Stack Requirements
- Next.js 15.3.4 with App Router
- React 19 with TypeScript (strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS v4 with shadcn/ui components
- Three.js v0.178.0 for 3D hero animation
- Framer Motion v12.23.3 and GSAP v3.13.0 for animations
- EmailJS v4.4.1 for contact form functionality

## Code Standards
- Always use TypeScript with strict mode enabled
- Follow existing component structure and established patterns
- Use descriptive, consistent naming conventions (camelCase for variables, PascalCase for components)
- Write clean, readable, and well-documented code with meaningful comments
- Prioritize accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA compliance) in all implementations
- Optimize for performance, especially Three.js animations and mobile devices

## Development Guidelines
- Mobile-first responsive design approach (breakpoints: 320px+, 768px+, 1024px+)
- Maintain existing design system and component architecture
- Use established patterns already present in the codebase
- Avoid introducing unnecessary dependencies or breaking changes
- Implement code splitting for Three.js components to improve performance
- Use lazy loading for non-critical animations and components

## Design Requirements
- Strictly follow reference images and design specifications
- All UI elements, spacing, colors, and typography must match designs exactly
- Maintain visual consistency across all breakpoints and devices
- Ensure smooth animations and interactions that enhance user experience
- Focus on professional presentation and modern web design principles

## Critical Implementation Notes
- Three.js animations must be performance-optimized and not impact page loading speed
- All components must be fully accessible with proper ARIA labels and keyboard navigation
- Code must be maintainable, extensible, and follow established architectural patterns
- Mobile optimization is crucial - test all features on mobile devices
- SEO optimization is required with proper meta tags and structured data# Ben Ko's Portfolio Website - Development Guidelines

